  "content": [
    {
      "text": "Six days shalt thou labour, and do all thy work, Ex. 20:9 (Deut. 5:13; Mosiah 13:17). Except the Lord build the house, they labour in vain, Ps. 127:1. thou shalt eat the labour of thine hands, Ps. 128:2. labour of the righteous tendeth to life, Prov. 10:16. he that gathereth by labour shall increase, Prov. 13:11. In all labour there is profit, Prov. 14:23. slothful … his hands refuse to labour, Prov. 21:25. make his soul enjoy good in his labour, Eccl. 2:24. sleep of a labouring man is sweet, Eccl. 5:12. to rejoice in his labour, Eccl. 5:19. ye spend … your labour for that which satisfieth not, Isa. 55:2. They shall not labour in vain, Isa. 65:23.",
