    {
      "text": "Come unto me, all ye that labour and are heavy laden, Matt. 11:28. Labour not for the meat which perisheth, John 6:27. these hands have ministered unto my necessities, Acts 20:34. that so labouring ye ought to support the weak, Acts 20:35. his own reward according to his own labour, 1 Cor. 3:8. labour, working with our own hands, 1 Cor. 4:12. steal no more: but rather let him labour, Eph. 4:28. your work of faith, and labour of love, 1 Thes. 1:3. labour and travail: for labouring night and day, 1 Thes. 2:9 (2 Thes. 3:8). we both labour and suffer reproach, 1 Tim. 4:10. Let us labour therefore to enter into that rest, Heb. 4:11. God is not unrighteous to forget your work and labour, Heb. 6:10. die in the Lord … they may rest from their labours, Rev. 14:13.",
