      "text": "labor which they had to perform was to look, 1 Ne. 17:41. Nephi, did cause my people … to labor with their hands, 2 Ne. 5:17. do not spend … your labor for that which cannot satisfy, 2 Ne. 9:51. laborer in Zion shall labor for Zion, 2 Ne. 26:31. Do they remember … the labors, and the pains of the Jews, 2 Ne. 29:4. by laboring with our might their blood might not come, Jacob 1:19. labor in the vineyard, with your might, Jacob 5:71 (5:15–70). labored with mine own hands that I might serve you, Mosiah 2:14. priests … labor with their own hands, Mosiah 18:24. laboring with their own hands for their support, Mosiah 27:4. they did all labor, every man according to his strength, Alma 1:26. rather than spend their days in idleness they would labor, Alma 24:18. they have labored exceedingly, Alma 29:15. I have labored … with mine own hands for my support, Alma 30:32 (32:5). we do not receive anything for our labors in the church, Alma 30:34. this life is the day for men to perform their labors, Alma 34:32. joy in the fruit of my labors, Alma 36:25. labor diligently; for if we should cease to labor … brought under condemnation; for we have a labor to perform, Moro. 9:6.",
